\line
\b\fs26\cf1 1. AIM OF THE EXPERIMENT\b0\fs22\cf0\par
1. To create a Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) and prepare a Gantt chart to illustrate project scheduling using Microsoft Excel.\par
2. To prepare a project Risk Register listing five major risks with their probability, impact, risk score (Probability x Impact), and mitigation plan.\par
\line
\b\fs26\cf1 2. THEORETICAL PRINCIPLES\b0\fs22\cf0\par
- \b Work Breakdown Structure (WBS):\b0  Hierarchical decomposition of total scope following the 100% rule.\par
- \b Gantt Chart:\b0  Timeline-based scheduling tool displaying start/end dates, dependencies, and 16 weekly intervals.\par
- \b Risk Management Formula:\b0  Risk Score = Probability (1 to 5) x Impact (1 to 5). Critical (16-25), High (10-15), Medium (5-9), Low (1-4).\par
\line
\b\fs26\cf1 3. EXCEL FORMULAS USED\b0\fs22\cf0\par
- Task Duration: \b =H6 - G6 + 1\b0  (Calculates total active calendar days between End Date and Start Date).\par
- Risk Score: \b =E6 * F6\b0  (Multiplies Probability in column E by Impact in column F).\par
- Risk Severity: \b =IF(G6>=16, "Critical", IF(G6>=10, "High", IF(G6>=5, "Medium", "Low")))\b0\par
